♪ We'll turn Manhattan ♪

65
00:04:28.529 --> 00:04:33.751
♪ Into an isle of joy

66
00:04:33.882 --> 00:04:36.276
[smooth jazz music fades]

67
00:04:38.452 --> 00:04:41.455
[birds chirping]
[squishing]

68
00:04:55.904 --> 00:04:57.166
Five minutes. honey.

69
00:04:58.646 --> 00:04:59.908
Yeah. I'm almost done.

70
00:05:00.996 --> 00:05:03.085
Luis said he's gonna quiz me
on this at the party.

71
00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:05.566
Thanks for usin' a drop cloth
this time

72
00:05:05.653 --> 00:05:06.654
instead of the tablecloth.

73
00:05:06.741 --> 00:05:07.655
[Hershel chuckles]

74
00:05:09.134 --> 00:05:12.834
[indistinct chattering]

75
00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.792
Come here.

76
00:05:14.923 --> 00:05:15.924
Hi.

77
00:05:18.187 --> 00:05:19.319
I brought you
a little somethin'.

78
00:05:21.538 --> 00:05:25.237
The last bag of French roast
from Bruegel's stash.

79
00:05:26.064 --> 00:05:28.284
I'm not sure if my wife's gonna
be happier to see me or this.

80
00:05:28.937 --> 00:05:31.026
- If she even recognizes you.
- [Armstrong chuckling]

81
00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.202
I appreciate it.

82
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.596
I really wish
you weren't leavin'.

83
00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.641
'Cause you're gonna
miss me so much?

84
00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:41.079
- I don't like it.
- I get it.

85
00:05:42.254 --> 00:05:43.647
You're worried you're
gonna lose this place.

86
00:05:44.213 --> 00:05:45.606
You and Renata really
got something here.

87
00:05:46.171 --> 00:05:47.129
It's made you different.

88
00:05:47.782 --> 00:05:49.914
Between us gettin' captured
and almost gettin' killed.

89
00:05:50.698 --> 00:05:52.439
I used to wonder what you
were like before all this.

90
00:05:52.569 --> 00:05:53.614
[chuckling]

91
00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:55.529
[Armstrong] Now I have some
idea.

92
00:05:55.616 --> 00:05:57.705
I'ma keep my mouth shut
about what you got here. Maggie.

93
00:05:58.662 --> 00:06:00.229
- You can trust me.
- I do...

94
00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:04.233
- And I don't.
- [Armstrong chuckling]

95
00:06:04.668 --> 00:06:06.670
Anybody on the road asks me
where I got this bag

96
00:06:06.757 --> 00:06:09.020
full of beans.
I'ma tell 'em the truth.

97
00:06:10.848 --> 00:06:12.023
Boston.

98
00:06:12.415 --> 00:06:14.243
[snickering]

99
00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.680
Look. I know it's your job
to protect this place. but.

100
00:06:16.811 --> 00:06:18.029
even if I did tell anyone.

101
00:06:18.595 --> 00:06:20.771
you'd see us rollin' in
from literally a mile away.

102
00:06:20.858 --> 00:06:23.818
Luis. por favor...

103
00:06:23.905 --> 00:06:26.821
Red light. everyone. red light.
You know what to do.

104
00:06:26.908 --> 00:06:28.388
Away from the windows.
Andale.

105
00:06:29.737 --> 00:06:32.783
[tense music]

106
00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.568
- I'll head up.
- Right behind you.

107
00:06:35.656 --> 00:06:40.574
[tense music continues]
[Dillard] [indistinct chatter]

108
00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.969
[Negan] Renata and Maggie are
at it again.

109
00:06:45.056 --> 00:06:51.106
[tense music continues]
[walkers snarling faintly]

110
00:06:54.805 --> 00:06:56.372
Looks like a couple of
your friends from New Babaloo.

111
00:06:56.503 --> 00:07:02.552
[tense music continues]

112
00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:05.033
Haven't seen
survivors in weeks.

113
00:07:05.512 --> 00:07:07.252
I wonder what the hell
they're doin' up here.

114
00:07:09.037 --> 00:07:10.081
[Maggie] You see anything?

115
00:07:10.995 --> 00:07:11.953
[Armstrong] No.

116
00:07:13.345 --> 00:07:14.869
[Linus] The Dama
needs food.

117
00:07:14.999 --> 00:07:16.218
[Reece]
We need food first!

118
00:07:16.348 --> 00:07:17.959
[Linus] No. no. no.
she needs it first.

119
00:07:18.089 --> 00:07:19.351
[Reece] I haven't eaten in
two days...

120
00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:20.483
They're tryin' to help someone.

121
00:07:20.614 --> 00:07:22.746
[Linus]
We feed her. She feeds us.

122
00:07:22.832 --> 00:07:26.184
The Dama feeds our minds.
our souls.

123
00:07:27.185 --> 00:07:29.187
[Dillard] Because we never
signed any notarized treaty

124
00:07:29.274 --> 00:07:30.362
to join their community.

125
00:07:30.711 --> 00:07:31.842
Hey. hey.

126
00:07:31.929 --> 00:07:34.932
I am asking him right now.
[shushing] Stop.

127
00:07:35.019 --> 00:07:36.368
[walker snarling]

128
00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:38.632
Titicaca wants to know
when the sweet jams can return.

129
00:07:38.936 --> 00:07:42.026
How many times I gotta ask you
to stop pretendin'

130
00:07:42.157 --> 00:07:44.202
like you can talk
to those toothless freaks?

131
00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:46.161
How many times do I gotta tell
you I can

132
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:47.467
decipher multiple phrases?
Desires.

133
00:07:48.206 --> 00:07:49.033
[Maggie] Negan. are you there?

134
00:07:49.164 --> 00:07:50.295
- [shushing]
- Okay.

135
00:07:53.429 --> 00:07:56.954
Deal's a deal: stop light
goes on. so does the walkie.

136
00:07:57.085 --> 00:07:59.087
See. I am a good little boy.

137
00:07:59.391 --> 00:08:00.828
You got eyeballs on these guys?

138
00:08:00.958 --> 00:08:02.220
It sounds like
they're over by you.

139
00:08:03.047 --> 00:08:06.442
Limpy McGee and Trotter?
Yeah. What are they sayin'?

140
00:08:06.529 --> 00:08:09.532
They're lookin' for food
for the Dama.

141
00:08:10.838 --> 00:08:13.928
Shit. the Dama eats?
I thought she just sucked blood.

142
00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:15.451
This is what
we've been waitin' for.

143
00:08:15.582 --> 00:08:17.148
Don't tell me that you're drunk.

144
00:08:17.235 --> 00:08:19.237
[Negan] No such thing.
Let's go get her.

145
00:08:19.324 --> 00:08:21.544
- [chuckling]
- [Dillard] Okay.

146
00:08:21.936 --> 00:08:23.241
Who is the Dama?

147
00:08:23.328 --> 00:08:26.506
She is a big dick
who's about to get hers.

148
00:08:26.636 --> 00:08:32.686
[theme music]
[walkers snarling]

149
00:09:21.648 --> 00:09:22.866
[tense music]

150
00:09:22.953 --> 00:09:24.172
[Negan] I gotta tell ya. man.

151
00:09:24.302 --> 00:09:25.390
I never thought we were gonna
get rid of ya.

152
00:09:26.435 --> 00:09:27.915
Actually wantin'
to be with my family?

153
00:09:28.002 --> 00:09:31.092
- I know it's a foreign concept.
- Ouch. Well. that stings.

154
00:09:32.093 --> 00:09:33.921
See? I'll tell you why.

155
00:09:34.051 --> 00:09:36.401
'Cause the sad truth is.
Annie and Joshua?

156
00:09:36.488 --> 00:09:38.012
They are better off without me.

157
00:09:38.142 --> 00:09:41.755
The happy truth is:
I'm better off without them.

158
00:09:43.147 --> 00:09:45.802
Livin' in a bar
that smells like rotting flesh.

159
00:09:45.889 --> 00:09:50.111
[tense music]

160
00:09:50.241 --> 00:09:51.068
Okay.

161
00:09:51.199 --> 00:09:53.897
[tense music continues]

162
00:09:54.028 --> 00:09:55.856
[Negan] Dama's Broadway babies!

163
00:09:55.943 --> 00:10:01.949
[tense music continues]

164
00:10:14.178 --> 00:10:17.181
[Linus] Who feeds us more
than merely bread?

165
00:10:17.965 --> 00:10:20.968
And fills our soul
and fills our head?

166
00:10:24.885 --> 00:10:27.975
Who kindles dreams o'er the day?

167
00:10:29.454 --> 00:10:31.805
Whose shining brilliance
guides the way?

168
00:10:34.459 --> 00:10:37.506
Who sees the future
like Nostradama?

169
00:10:38.594 --> 00:10:42.685
Who indeed. but our fair Dama?

170
00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:46.820
[Negan clapping]

171
00:10:47.211 --> 00:10:50.824
Well. Holy Jesus.

172
00:10:50.954 --> 00:10:54.349
I have taken
more poetic shits than that.

173
00:10:54.915 --> 00:10:56.003
We're not here to hurt you.

174
00:10:57.961 --> 00:10:58.832
[Negan] That. though?

175
00:10:59.963 --> 00:11:01.704
I mean. I'm not much
of a painting guy.

176
00:11:01.835 --> 00:11:04.664
but those are some
sweet-ass boobies.

177
00:11:07.057 --> 00:11:09.581
These are the two
hilltops of kinship.

178
00:11:09.669 --> 00:11:11.583
Together. they form
the foundation of civilized...

179
00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:12.976
[Negan] No. no. no. no. no. no.

180
00:11:13.107 --> 00:11:14.935
Those are boobies.

181
00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.633
Have you ever seen
an honest to God...

182
00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.591
- Are you done?
- [Negan] Well. no.

183
00:11:19.722 --> 00:11:22.246
I mean. look. those are some
hot alien boobies.

184
00:11:22.986 --> 00:11:25.293
We saw you scavenging.
We brought food.

185
00:11:26.598 --> 00:11:29.166
We have more food at home
than you could eat.

186
00:11:29.906 --> 00:11:32.169
We have a doctor. too.
He can set you right.

187
00:11:32.692 --> 00:11:34.215
I'm headin' back
to New Babylon tomorrow.

188
00:11:35.172 --> 00:11:38.001
If you'd rather come home.
there's room on my boat.

189
00:11:38.349 --> 00:11:39.611
Sounds amazing.

190
00:11:40.482 --> 00:11:42.353
A bunch of strangers
who wanna help us

191
00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:44.138
and who don't want
anything from us?

192
00:11:44.268 --> 00:11:46.401
We just want you
to tell us where the Dama is.

193
00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:50.753
- That's all you have to do.
- [Dama] I saved these men.

194
00:11:51.275 --> 00:11:52.233
They were injured.

195
00:11:52.363 --> 00:11:54.975
Not just their bodies.
their minds.

196
00:11:55.062 --> 00:11:57.412
They couldn't dream.
I fixed them.

197
00:11:57.499 --> 00:11:59.457
But the first thing
that you dream is

198
00:11:59.588 --> 00:12:02.722
not to let anyonestop
you from dreaming.

199
00:12:03.505 --> 00:12:07.030
You stopped Hershel.
But you didn't stop me.

200
00:12:07.161 --> 00:12:08.902
And you can't stop them.

201
00:12:09.206 --> 00:12:13.167
Oh. yeah. I mean. however
are we gonna stop them?

202
00:12:14.081 --> 00:12:15.996
Leave now. You'll live.

203
00:12:16.083 --> 00:12:17.606
[Dama] But your dreams will die.

204
00:12:18.041 --> 00:12:19.477
- [Armstrong] Damn it.
- You are gonna get

205
00:12:19.608 --> 00:12:20.740
these boys killed!

206
00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:23.003
[Dama]
"Once more unto the breach.

207
00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.005
"dear friends. once more;

208
00:12:25.092 --> 00:12:27.659
or close them all up
with our English dead."

209
00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:30.401
- Go now! Please!
- [Dama] "In peace..."

210
00:12:30.662 --> 00:12:31.707
Drop your weapons.

211
00:12:31.794 --> 00:12:33.578
"There's nothing
so becomes a man

212
00:12:33.709 --> 00:12:36.190
as modest stillness
and humility."

213
00:12:36.277 --> 00:12:37.582
Please just turn around.

214
00:12:37.669 --> 00:12:38.714
- [Maggie] All of you.
- [Dama] "But. when

215
00:12:38.845 --> 00:12:40.629
the blast of war..."
[gunshot]

216
00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.631
- God damn it!
- Drop your weapons!

217
00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:44.546
[Dama] "Stiffen the sinews..."
[gunshots]

218
00:12:44.676 --> 00:12:45.765
[Dama] "Summon up the blood..."

219
00:12:45.895 --> 00:12:50.204
[gunshots]
[dramatic music]

220
00:12:52.423 --> 00:12:53.903
God. that was stupid!

221
00:12:54.512 --> 00:12:59.779
[dramatic music continues]

222
00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.128
Go.

223
00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:04.131
- [Maggie] Go!
- [whimpering]

224
00:13:05.045 --> 00:13:05.959
[Dama] Fight!

225
00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:07.482
Fight. you coward!

226
00:13:07.612 --> 00:13:10.964
[dramatic music]

227
00:13:11.051 --> 00:13:12.443
There.

228
00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:15.620
[dramatic music continues]

229
00:13:15.707 --> 00:13:18.275
- It's over. Dama.
- [Dama] The end is

230
00:13:18.406 --> 00:13:21.017
never really the end.

231
00:13:21.104 --> 00:13:22.105
[rope creaks. snaps]

232
00:13:22.236 --> 00:13:23.628
[Armstrong] Look out!

233
00:13:23.715 --> 00:13:24.934
[bodies thudding]

234
00:13:25.065 --> 00:13:26.153
[chandelier crashing]

235
00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:27.154
[dramatic music continues]

236
00:13:27.284 --> 00:13:28.372
[Negan groaning]

237
00:13:28.459 --> 00:13:30.331
Son of a bitch. [groans]

238
00:13:30.461 --> 00:13:33.595
There she goes. Get up! Hurry!

239
00:13:33.725 --> 00:13:36.816
[dramatic music continues]

240
00:13:39.296 --> 00:13:41.821
- [walker snarling]
- [screaming] No!

241
00:13:41.908 --> 00:13:43.387
[walker growling]

242
00:13:43.474 --> 00:13:45.955
- [Dama groaning]
- [walker snarling]

243
00:13:46.086 --> 00:13:49.698
[dramatic music continues]

244
00:13:49.785 --> 00:13:53.006
[blade squelching]
[Dama panting]

245
00:13:56.226 --> 00:13:59.708
[tense music]
[Maggie panting]

246
00:14:00.622 --> 00:14:03.364
[panting] You selfish swine!

247
00:14:04.365 --> 00:14:05.757
Your son...

248
00:14:05.888 --> 00:14:09.196
was gonna shape
the future of this city.

249
00:14:10.675 --> 00:14:12.808
But you couldn't let that
happen.

250
00:14:12.939 --> 00:14:14.723
You had to lure him away.

251
00:14:16.638 --> 00:14:18.858
I will see Hershel again.
and when I do.

252
00:14:19.249 --> 00:14:21.817
he will understand the error
of his ways.

253
00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.385
[Negan] Sure.

254
00:14:25.125 --> 00:14:27.736
Keep talkin'... Please.

255
00:14:27.823 --> 00:14:29.085
[Armstrong]
You don't need to kill her.

256
00:14:29.172 --> 00:14:30.043
[Negan] Oh. no.

257
00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:32.523
She absolutely needs to die.

258
00:14:32.654 --> 00:14:34.177
[suspenseful music]
No!

259
00:14:34.264 --> 00:14:35.570
[gunshot]
[bullet whizzing]

260
00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:40.880
[tense music]

261
00:14:46.842 --> 00:14:49.714
[wind blowing]
[birds chirping]

262
00:14:49.845 --> 00:14:53.544
[metal rattling]
[walkers growling]

263
00:14:54.415 --> 00:14:58.767
[walkers growling faintly]

264
00:15:01.161 --> 00:15:02.379
[Dama] Where's The Croat?

265
00:15:03.641 --> 00:15:05.426
He obviously built
these for you.

266
00:15:05.513 --> 00:15:06.906
Where is he?

267
00:15:07.471 --> 00:15:08.908
Dead.

268
00:15:11.954 --> 00:15:13.913
Th... and where
did you get these tanks?

269
00:15:17.394 --> 00:15:20.920
[tense music]

270
00:15:23.183 --> 00:15:24.271
Eat.

271
00:15:25.228 --> 00:15:26.447
Not in here.

272
00:15:28.144 --> 00:15:29.406
I can't be in here.

273
00:15:31.887 --> 00:15:33.106
Why haven't you killed me yet?

274
00:15:33.497 --> 00:15:37.762
[tense music continues]
[walkers snarling faintly]

275
00:15:37.849 --> 00:15:38.938
Maggie...

276
00:15:42.028 --> 00:15:43.943
I... I... I might have...

277
00:15:44.421 --> 00:15:45.683
...underestimated you.

278
00:15:46.467 --> 00:15:50.123
Maybe you are where
Hershel gets his spark.

279
00:15:51.472 --> 00:15:52.821
I wanna help. Maggie.

280
00:15:53.213 --> 00:15:55.606
I want this city to be restored.

281
00:15:56.172 --> 00:15:59.697
It's all I've ever wanted.
This hospital was a

282
00:15:59.828 --> 00:16:03.440
great start.
but you need to think bigger.

283
00:16:04.224 --> 00:16:09.794
Enough of these tanks.
you can power this whole island.

284
00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.189
We just need to talk
about it more.

285
00:16:13.755 --> 00:16:17.106
So I can paint pictures for you?

286
00:16:18.151 --> 00:16:20.327
So I can kill for you?

287
00:16:20.805 --> 00:16:25.332
I had a vision.
I have knowledge.

288
00:16:26.115 --> 00:16:28.639
Central Park used
to be farmland.

289
00:16:28.726 --> 00:16:31.686
These lofts. factories...

290
00:16:33.514 --> 00:16:38.171
There's an entire civilization
just waiting to be unleashed.

291
00:16:39.563 --> 00:16:40.869
There is.

292
00:16:44.307 --> 00:16:45.178
Maggie!

293
00:16:45.656 --> 00:16:46.657
Maggie!

294
00:16:47.049 --> 00:16:48.964
[walkers snarling]

295
00:16:49.095 --> 00:16:51.488
[tense music continues]

296
00:16:51.575 --> 00:16:55.579
[tray clattering]
[walkers growling]

297
00:16:55.665 --> 00:16:58.582
[paper rustling]

298
00:16:58.713 --> 00:17:00.193
- I don't think I'm ready yet.
- [Luis] You are.

299
00:17:01.977 --> 00:17:04.719
Remember:
one breath. one motion.

300
00:17:05.241 --> 00:17:06.634
[Negan] Hey!

301
00:17:06.763 --> 00:17:09.897
Somebody get me a goddamn
needle. I'll do it myself!

302
00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:15.164
It's just skin.
His is obviously very thin.

303
00:17:16.686 --> 00:17:22.737
[skin squelching]
[Negan groaning]

304
00:17:23.954 --> 00:17:29.309
[Negan sighing]
[skin squelching]

305
00:17:29.396 --> 00:17:32.051
So glad I get to be. like.
your practice dummy here.

306
00:17:34.966 --> 00:17:36.403
What the hell are
you even doin' here?

307
00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:38.274
What does it look like?

308
00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:43.323
I'm watchin' my son put a needle
through your flesh repeatedly.

309
00:17:44.193 --> 00:17:45.412
Why don't you go get your son.
like.

310
00:17:45.542 --> 00:17:47.109
a shot of hooch
to calm his nerves?

311
00:17:47.196 --> 00:17:48.632
Just 'cause you
don't like needles.

312
00:17:48.763 --> 00:17:50.547
you don't have to take
it out on him.

313
00:17:50.634 --> 00:17:52.027
Oh. yeah.
Obviously. I have a real

314
00:17:52.114 --> 00:17:54.595
aversion to needles.
needle dick.

315
00:17:57.163 --> 00:17:58.729
Look. Sparky...

316
00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:02.124
I have saved
your life multiple times.

317
00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.300
Why are you scared of me?

318
00:18:04.387 --> 00:18:06.215
Why would anyone be
weirded out by the dude who

319
00:18:06.302 --> 00:18:07.695
spends all day
playing video games

320
00:18:07.782 --> 00:18:09.088
in his walker bar?

321
00:18:10.393 --> 00:18:11.786
I mean. how'd you even get this?

322
00:18:12.743 --> 00:18:13.875
One of those empty
bottles of yours

323
00:18:14.005 --> 00:18:15.398
try to jump out and bite ya?

324
00:18:18.445 --> 00:18:19.402
He doesn't know?

325
00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:24.494
[gentle music]

326
00:18:24.581 --> 00:18:28.411
She's downstairs.
She's locked up.

327
00:18:30.892 --> 00:18:33.982
She is never gonna hurt you.
I promise.

328
00:18:34.591 --> 00:18:36.637
There's no need to be afraid.

329
00:18:38.247 --> 00:18:40.031
I know this is wrong. but...

330
00:18:41.337 --> 00:18:45.124
I think if I was there. I would
have wanted to kill her. but...

331
00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:48.127
Everybody in
the room wanted that.

332
00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.304
But I don't know if I could've.

333
00:18:52.827 --> 00:18:57.484
[inhales sharply] Sometimes
I worry. you know.

334
00:18:57.614 --> 00:18:59.355
when it's my time
to kill a person.

335
00:19:00.139 --> 00:19:01.792
that I won't be able to do it.

336
00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:07.320
Is that somethin'
you can teach me?

337
00:19:08.538 --> 00:19:12.803
[music intensifies]

338
00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.589
So realistically.
what are our options here?

339
00:19:15.676 --> 00:19:17.417
What?
We really just have two?

340
00:19:17.504 --> 00:19:19.723
Kill her or keep her locked
up for the rest of her life?

341
00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.464
Or we could try
to rehabilitate her.

342
00:19:21.551 --> 00:19:24.772
- You ever seen that work?
- Yeah. I have.

343
00:19:24.859 --> 00:19:26.339
You think it'll work with her?

344
00:19:26.687 --> 00:19:28.254
- I don't know.
- [Renata] Okay.

345
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.128
If we keep her locked up in
jail. we are using resources.

346
00:19:33.215 --> 00:19:34.608
And I'm not just
talking about food.

347
00:19:34.738 --> 00:19:37.045
If we're sayin' that she
is so dangerous that she can't

348
00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:38.438
be outside of a cage.

349
00:19:38.525 --> 00:19:40.570
then we need someone
to guard her to make sure

350
00:19:40.657 --> 00:19:42.181
that she never gets
outta that cage

351
00:19:42.572 --> 00:19:44.922
and probably another guard
guarding the first guard.

352
00:19:45.053 --> 00:19:46.837
since we clearly can't
leave her alone with anyone.

353
00:19:47.925 --> 00:19:49.449
Or we kill her.

354
00:19:49.579 --> 00:19:52.539
And all we lose are the values
we built this community on.

355
00:19:53.279 --> 00:19:57.065
[Negan] Bulllllllll shiiiiiit.

356
00:19:58.719 --> 00:20:01.678
[scoffing] Excuse me?

357
00:20:02.331 --> 00:20:05.204
Look. if the values
of this community are keeping

358
00:20:05.291 --> 00:20:08.250
a murderer around.
then best of luck to you.

359
00:20:08.381 --> 00:20:10.687
[Renata. scoffing]
I know for a fact

360
00:20:10.774 --> 00:20:13.037
that you have killed innocent
people.

361
00:20:13.124 --> 00:20:15.823
- Should we just kill you. too?
- [Negan] Yeah.

362
00:20:15.953 --> 00:20:17.477
See. the issue here is...

363
00:20:17.607 --> 00:20:22.003
I am not in your community.
See. I reside in Fuck-you-ville.

364
00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:24.266
ZIP code: Fuck you.

365
00:20:24.353 --> 00:20:26.660
Nothing lasts unless you are

366
00:20:26.747 --> 00:20:29.619
willing to do the most
brutal shit imaginable

367
00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:33.449
to keep it. and that. my friend.
that ain't you.

368
00:20:34.015 --> 00:20:36.844
You are correct. That ain't me.

369
00:20:37.801 --> 00:20:40.761
And if that is a problem
for you. then congratulations.

370
00:20:40.848 --> 00:20:42.937
You definitely made
the right call hiding out

371
00:20:43.024 --> 00:20:44.417
in that stinky bar of yours.

372
00:20:47.071 --> 00:20:48.072
Look...

373
00:20:48.856 --> 00:20:51.859
you can go downstairs and kill
the lady that wanted to kill

374
00:20:51.946 --> 00:20:55.297
you and Hershel or you can
listen to this lady

375
00:20:55.384 --> 00:20:57.081
who's gonna get you
and Hershel killed.

376
00:20:58.387 --> 00:21:00.171
[Negan] It's your call.
[tense music]

377
00:21:00.259 --> 00:21:05.307
[bat knocking]
[tense music continues]

378
00:21:05.394 --> 00:21:08.267
I know the Dama.
and Negan knows her. too.

379
00:21:09.746 --> 00:21:12.575
We have all been
terrorized by her.

380
00:21:13.707 --> 00:21:15.839
What she had the Croat do to us?

381
00:21:17.145 --> 00:21:21.236
No one makes the right decision
when they're scared or angry.

382
00:21:21.323 --> 00:21:25.545
And I... I am really trying
to hold the light here. Maggie.

383
00:21:25.632 --> 00:21:30.376
I really am. but...
I don't know if I can.

384
00:21:30.463 --> 00:21:34.293
May not have to.
She's not eating.

385
00:21:34.554 --> 00:21:36.033
I was just down there

386
00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:37.687
and she looks like she's been
malnourished for a while.

387
00:21:38.122 --> 00:21:41.691
She keeps up this hunger strike.
she won't last for long.

388
00:21:42.779 --> 00:21:44.477
Then maybe we let her
make the decision.

389
00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:47.654
I mean.
if she's set on killin' herself

390
00:21:47.784 --> 00:21:49.699
in the most
painful way possible.

391
00:21:50.047 --> 00:21:51.310
starvin' herself to death?

392
00:21:52.311 --> 00:21:54.443
I don't see anything wrong
with givin' her another option.

393
00:21:55.966 --> 00:21:57.664
It doesn't have to be slow.

394
00:22:03.496 --> 00:22:05.062
Just do me a favor
and drop it.

395
00:22:05.149 --> 00:22:06.586
How can I drop it. okay?

396
00:22:06.977 --> 00:22:08.022
If you're sayin'
I can't understand.

397
00:22:08.152 --> 00:22:09.284
them. you're sayin' I'm a liar.

398
00:22:09.371 --> 00:22:11.591
No. what I am saying is stop
pretendin' like

399
00:22:11.678 --> 00:22:12.896
- you can understand...
- Again with the pretending.

400
00:22:13.027 --> 00:22:13.897
I'm not pretending.

401
00:22:13.984 --> 00:22:15.682
- I am...
- [walker snarling]

402
00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:18.902
- I'm adapting.
- Jesus Christ.

403
00:22:18.989 --> 00:22:21.035
- No...
- Hold on. it's okay. It's okay.

404
00:22:22.732 --> 00:22:25.344
[walker growling]

405
00:22:27.258 --> 00:22:30.653
- [walker snarling]
- [Dillard groans like walker]

406
00:22:30.740 --> 00:22:35.049
[walker snarling]

407
00:22:36.572 --> 00:22:37.704
His name is Chaz.

408
00:22:38.357 --> 00:22:40.881
Hey. don't poke the bear.

409
00:22:42.796 --> 00:22:45.842
[walker growling]

410
00:22:47.191 --> 00:22:49.542
[Dillard groaning like a walker]

411
00:22:49.629 --> 00:22:52.240
[walker groaning]

412
00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:54.938
[metal rattling]
[walker growling]

413
00:22:55.025 --> 00:22:57.071
- [walker snarling]
- Okay...

414
00:23:01.292 --> 00:23:02.946
Poor bastard's a Jets fan.

415
00:23:03.077 --> 00:23:04.208
[walker growling]

416
00:23:04.295 --> 00:23:05.862
[metal rattling]

417
00:23:05.949 --> 00:23:07.124
[walker snarling]

418
00:23:07.255 --> 00:23:08.387
Get outta my way.

419
00:23:08.517 --> 00:23:09.431
[walker growling]
[cracking]

420
00:23:09.518 --> 00:23:10.780
[metal rattling]

421
00:23:10.867 --> 00:23:13.217
[metal creaking]

422
00:23:13.304 --> 00:23:14.784
[Negan] Move!

423
00:23:14.915 --> 00:23:16.264
[thudding]

424
00:23:16.786 --> 00:23:22.270
[glass shattering]
[walkers snarling]

425
00:23:22.792 --> 00:23:24.751
[Dillard] Damn c'mon!
Let's go. let's go. let's go!

426
00:23:24.838 --> 00:23:26.927
- [Negan] Up this way!
- [walkers snarling]

427
00:23:28.668 --> 00:23:29.799
[Dillard] Move!

428
00:23:29.886 --> 00:23:33.194
[tense music]

429
00:23:33.281 --> 00:23:35.631
- You good?
- [walkers snarling]

430
00:23:35.718 --> 00:23:39.113
[Negan sighs]
You're not funny.

431
00:23:39.243 --> 00:23:40.593
[panting]

432
00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:45.815
[walkers growling]

433
00:23:45.946 --> 00:23:49.993
[brick thudding]
These fuckers. they have teeth.

434
00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:53.083
[brick thudding]
And nails.

435
00:23:53.214 --> 00:23:56.086
[thudding]
They aren't your little pets

436
00:23:56.173 --> 00:23:57.523
at the bar.

437
00:23:57.610 --> 00:24:01.309
They are death on two feet.
Do you hear me?

438
00:24:01.396 --> 00:24:03.485
- [walkers snarling]
- Yeah.

439
00:24:03.616 --> 00:24:05.095
[Negan] I can't believe

440
00:24:05.182 --> 00:24:09.491
I even have to say this at all
after all these... years.

441
00:24:09.622 --> 00:24:13.930
[skin squelching]
[walker snarling]

442
00:24:14.017 --> 00:24:15.932
[Negan groaning]

443
00:24:17.934 --> 00:24:19.283
[Negan groaning]

444
00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:22.112
- [Negan grunting]
- [walker snarling]

445
00:24:22.199 --> 00:24:23.636
[walker roaring]
[air conditioner thudding]

446
00:24:23.723 --> 00:24:25.638
[skin squelching]

447
00:24:25.768 --> 00:24:27.814
[tense music]
You pull somethin'

448
00:24:27.901 --> 00:24:31.861
like that again. I will chat
you up with a tire iron.

449
00:24:31.948 --> 00:24:37.998
- [Dillard panting]
- [Negan groaning]

450
00:24:39.173 --> 00:24:41.088
[Dillard panting]

451
00:24:41.175 --> 00:24:44.352
- Hey...
- [Negan sighing]

452
00:24:46.006 --> 00:24:49.966
[groaning like a walker]. that's
how deadies say "I'm sorry."

453
00:24:50.619 --> 00:24:53.187
[Dillard panting]
[tense music continues]

454
00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:59.846
[gentle music]

455
00:25:17.385 --> 00:25:20.519
I used to be a cop.
I used to work undercover.

456
00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:25.045
When you go deep. it's not you.
you know?

457
00:25:28.570 --> 00:25:30.529
But it is. right?

458
00:25:32.400 --> 00:25:34.533
Whoever you are. it's not.
But it has to be.

459
00:25:35.969 --> 00:25:38.362
And for years.
when I went dark. it was me.

460
00:25:39.059 --> 00:25:39.973
And it was someone else.

461
00:25:40.887 --> 00:25:43.237
I'm holed up
in that bar for ages.

462
00:25:44.325 --> 00:25:45.239
I knew I didn't understand 'em.

463
00:25:47.415 --> 00:25:49.069
I had to pretend
or I would've gone crazy.

464
00:25:50.505 --> 00:25:51.680
Shit. maybe I did. I don't know.

465
00:25:51.767 --> 00:25:53.552
Maybe I don't
really know what is happenin'.

466
00:25:57.033 --> 00:25:58.078
I do know one thing.

467
00:25:58.165 --> 00:26:01.777
[gentle music]

468
00:26:01.864 --> 00:26:03.083
When you play
a part for too long.

469
00:26:03.213 --> 00:26:04.432
it becomes a piece
of who you are.

470
00:26:06.608 --> 00:26:10.264
And no matter what. there is no
way it's ever gonna leave you.

471
00:26:13.615 --> 00:26:15.617
So a part of me is always gonna
be the guy that had

472
00:26:15.748 --> 00:26:20.056
to unload shipping containers
full of girls.

473
00:26:20.143 --> 00:26:25.192
[somber music]

474
00:26:25.322 --> 00:26:27.063
And a piece of me is always
gonna understand them.

475
00:26:36.595 --> 00:26:37.596
It's fuckin' boobies.

476
00:26:40.903 --> 00:26:43.950
[tense music]

477
00:26:47.780 --> 00:26:50.217
I talked to the doctor.
I'm not eating.

478
00:26:50.870 --> 00:26:52.828
- I will not be here.
- I know.

479
00:26:52.915 --> 00:26:58.965
[tense music continues]

480
00:27:06.668 --> 00:27:08.931
I stood across from Negan
when he was in a cell.

481
00:27:10.716 --> 00:27:11.847
He wanted me to kill him.

482
00:27:11.978 --> 00:27:14.894
and I didn't
'cause I wanted him to suffer.

483
00:27:15.808 --> 00:27:19.463
I'm not gonna kill you
and I don't want you to suffer.

484
00:27:20.377 --> 00:27:22.815
You aren't gettin' out of here.
okay?

485
00:27:25.252 --> 00:27:27.297
But you can share the things
that you know.

486
00:27:28.995 --> 00:27:30.823
You can try to make up
for what you've done.

487
00:27:31.824 --> 00:27:32.781
You can change.

488
00:27:36.437 --> 00:27:37.351
Take a bite.

489
00:27:39.570 --> 00:27:43.183
Or don't... There's the knife.

490
00:27:46.229 --> 00:27:47.100
It is your choice.

491
00:27:47.187 --> 00:27:53.193
[tense music continues]

492
00:28:04.944 --> 00:28:07.860
[wind gusting]

493
00:28:16.129 --> 00:28:18.174
[Dillard shuts door]

494
00:28:18.261 --> 00:28:20.699
[Negan] Hey... Ah?

495
00:28:22.526 --> 00:28:23.527
I put 'em away.

496
00:28:26.182 --> 00:28:29.185
They're in my room.
I needed... needed a break.

497
00:28:31.187 --> 00:28:32.536
I think I'll be...
[clearing throat]

